import Mathlib.Data.List.Basic

/-!
# Certificates for the window lemma

A colouring of the subsets of an `11`-element set that depends only on the size of the set is
a word `g 0, g 1, …, g 11` of colours. For each such word with `g 0 = false` the list `certs`
below contains a sublattice of `2^{[11]}` whose member sizes all receive one colour `c` under
`g`, and which has more members than there are levels `v ≤ 11` with `g v = c`. A sublattice is
written as a list of bit masks below `2^11`; the second component lists the sizes that occur.

`certs_ok` checks that every listed family is closed under `|||` and `&&&` (union and
intersection of the corresponding sets) and that the sizes are as stated, and `cover_ok` checks
that every word is covered. Both are checked by evaluation in the kernel.
-/

namespace Erdos1183

/-- The number of the bits `0, …, 10` of `m` that are set. -/
def pc (m : ℕ) : ℕ := (List.range 11).countP fun i => m.testBit i

/-- The list of masks `l` is closed under `|||` and `&&&`. -/
def closedB (l : List ℕ) : Bool :=
  l.all fun a => l.all fun b => l.contains (a ||| b) && l.contains (a &&& b)

